                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>The rebound hyperacidity of the antacids can contribute to the development of chronic problems like dysplastic changes in the oesophagus (called Barrett's disease or Barrett's Oesophagus)&nbsp;</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>The rebound hyperacidity may contribute to the development of a peptic ulcer</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>The client may not get proper medical advice, resulting in the advancement of dysplastic changes in the oesophagus</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Antacids taken incorrectly can affect the absorption of some nutrients, resulting in nutritional deficiencies.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                }
